WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:06.022
Somewhere in your store, old stock is hiding behind new stock.

00:00:06.302 --> 00:00:08.616
A flow rack fixes that using gravity.

00:00:09.216 --> 00:00:14.143
On flat shelves, the newest stock goes in front and the oldest gets pushed to the back.

00:00:14.422 --> 00:00:17.099
It ages, gets damaged, or is forgotten.

00:00:17.379 --> 00:00:21.426
Then someone has to unload a whole shelf just to reach one box.

00:00:22.026 --> 00:00:24.099
A flow rack has sloped roller shelves.

00:00:24.379 --> 00:00:26.810
You load full bins at the back, the high end.

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:31.560
Gravity rolls them forward to the front, the low end, where the operator picks.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.295
The oldest stock is always first in line.

00:00:34.575 --> 00:00:36.889
This is FIFO: first in, first out.

00:00:37.169 --> 00:00:41.001
Keep the rollers clear of tape and debris, so the boxes keep flowing.

00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:48.085
A Furnisys Link Flow Rack carries 800 kilos, with 270 kilos per roller shelf.

00:00:48.365 --> 00:00:53.528
A shirt maker replaced disorganised storage with three Link flow racks for fabric,

00:00:53.528 --> 00:00:54.724
buttons and labels.

00:00:55.324 --> 00:00:57.669
Let gravity manage your stock rotation.

00:00:57.949 --> 00:01:00.316
What material ages fastest in your store?

00:01:00.596 --> 00:01:03.694
Comment below, and next, see how trolleys feed the line.

00:01:04.294 --> 00:01:08.539
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

